</code></pre><figcaption><p><span>Replace names in the schema Code</span></p></figcaption></figure><p><u>Benchmark after Flattened Schema + Improved System Prompt containing Schema Summary + Function Names Optimised </u><a href="https://github.com/SamparkAI/fcalling-clickup-blog-code/blob/master/main_flattened_sysprompt3_schemaOptimize.ipynb?ref=blog.composio.dev"><u>[Code Here]</u></a></p><figure><img src="https://blog.composio.dev/content/images/2024/03/image-4-1.png" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1300" height="284" srcset="https://blog.composio.dev/content/images/size/w600/2024/03/image-4-1.png 600w, https://blog.composio.dev/content/images/size/w1000/2024/03/image-4-1.png 1000w, https://blog.composio.dev/content/images/2024/03/image-4-1.png 1300w" sizes="(min-width: 720px) 720px"></figure><h2 id="optimising-function-description"><u>Optimising Function Description</u></h2><p>Here, we focus on the function descriptions and make those more clear and focused.</p><figure><pre><code>schema_func_decription_dict = {
    "get_spaces": "Retrives information of all the spaces available in user's Clickup Workspace.",
    "create_space": "Creates a new ClickUp space",
