    optimized_schema.append(temp_dict)
</code></pre><figcaption><p><span>Changing Schema</span></p></figcaption></figure><p><u>Benchmark after Flattened Schema + Improved System Prompt containing Schema Summary + Function Names Optimised + Function Descriptions Optimised</u> <a href="https://github.com/SamparkAI/fcalling-clickup-blog-code/blob/master/main_flattened_sysprompt3_schemaOptimize2.ipynb?ref=blog.composio.dev"><em>[Code Here]</em></a></p><figure><img src="https://blog.composio.dev/content/images/2024/03/image-3-1.png" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1313" height="286" srcset="https://blog.composio.dev/content/images/size/w600/2024/03/image-3-1.png 600w, https://blog.composio.dev/content/images/size/w1000/2024/03/image-3-1.png 1000w, https://blog.composio.dev/content/images/2024/03/image-3-1.png 1313w" sizes="(min-width: 720px) 720px"></figure><h2 id="optimising-gpt-function-parameter-descriptions"><u>Optimising gpt Function Parameter Descriptions</u></h2><p>Earlier, we flattened the schema by stacking nested parameters' descriptions with their parents' descriptions until they were in a flattened state. </p><p>Let's now replace them with:</p><pre><code>schema_func_params_dict = {
